---
date added: 2026-11-20
title: Olive Oil Pumpkin Cake With Salted Maple Cream
author: Andy Baraghani
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1027478-olive-oil-pumpkin-cake-with-salted-maple-cream
tags: cake, dessert, pumpkin, olive oil, maple, thanksgiving, fall, make-ahead
servings: 8
time required: 1 hour 30 minutes
cook time: 1 hour 15 minutes
notes: "If pumpkin pie feels tired, this cake is the upgrade: It's plush and deeply spiced without veering into heaviness, the kind of dessert that feels just as welcome at a holiday table as it does on a random Tuesday night. The salted maple whipped cream is what makes it sing, adding a cool, fluffy richness to balance the spice. (Sneak some bites but please, do your best to get as much of it onto the cake as possible.) Like most oil-based cakes, this pumpkin cake actually improves with time, so don't hesitate to bake it a day ahead; the flavors settle in and the crumb gets even more tender."
---

Make the cake: Heat the oven to 350 degrees. Lightly oil a #9-inch springform pan{} with @extra-virgin olive oil{}(plus more for pan) and line the bottom with #parchment paper{}.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{2.25%cups}(274 grams), @ground cinnamon{1%tablespoon}, @baking powder{2%teaspoons}, @freshly grated nutmeg{2%teaspoons}, @kosher salt{0.75%teaspoon}(such as Diamond Crystal) and @baking soda{0.5%teaspoon} in a medium #bowl{} to remove any lumps.

Using a #stand mixer{} with a paddle attachment (or electric hand mixer) on high speed, beat the @sugar{1%cup}(195 grams) and @large eggs{3}(room temperature) until very pale and thick and the mixture forms ribbons back on itself when lifted, ~{3-4%minutes}. (This may take longer if using a hand mixer.) Add the @canned pumpkin purée{1.5%cups}(345 grams) in two batches, beating on low until combined.

With the mixer still on low, gradually stream in the @extra-virgin olive oil{0.75%cup}(177 milliliters), then beat in the @vanilla extract{2%teaspoons}. The batter should look a little thicker.

Working in two batches, add the dry ingredients and mix on low speed, stopping and scraping down sides in between, until no streaks remain. Scrape the batter into the prepared pan and smooth the top. Bake until the top is firm and a tester inserted into the center comes out clean, ~{40-50%minutes}.

Let the cake cool in the pan on a #wire rack{} for ~{15%minutes}, then run a knife around the edge and release. Cool completely for at least ~{1%hour} before serving. (If working ahead, wrap the cake entirely in plastic and store at room temperature for up to 3 days, until ready to serve.)

Just before serving, make the whipped cream: Use a stand mixer with the whisk attachment, hand mixer or just a plain #whisk{} (yes!) to beat the @heavy cream{1.5%cups}(355 milliliters) until you reach soft, floppy peaks. Add the @sour cream{0.5%cup}(115 grams), @maple syrup{3%tablespoons} and a pinch of @kosher salt{} and whisk to nearly stiff peaks.

Using a #rubber spatula{}, plop the cream onto the cooled cake and spread it out, keeping some swoops and waves. Drizzle with more @maple syrup{}(for drizzling) and finish with @flaky salt{}(optional) just before serving, if you like.
